  "partners": {
    "title": "Partners",
    "seo": "BuildNinja Partners | Help Teams Deliver Software",
    "description": "Explore BuildNinja partnerships for consultants, integrators, service providers, and technology companies working with self-hosted CI/CD.",
    "content": "### Help your customers take control of their build workflow.\n\nBring BuildNinja into the conversations you already have about software delivery, infrastructure, and developer productivity.\n\nTogether, we can explore how self-hosted CI/CD with AI built in fits the teams you serve.\n\n**Primary action:** Discuss a partnership  \n**Alternative:** [Explore BuildNinja](https://www.buildninja.io/features)\n\n### Built around the work you do.\n\n#### DevOps and cloud consultants\n\nHelp customers evaluate, configure, and operate a build environment that fits their delivery needs.\n\n#### Software and product companies\n\nExplore how BuildNinja can fit the development workflows and solutions you support.\n\n#### System integrators\n\nConnect the build workflow with a customer's repositories, infrastructure, identity, and deployment tools.\n\n#### Managed service providers\n\nDiscuss how BuildNinja could fit the environments and engineering services you manage for customers.\n\n### Find a way to work together.\n\n| Partnership opportunity | What we can explore |\n| --- | --- |\n| Referrals and resale | Introduce customers with a relevant need and discuss the right commercial model. |\n| Integrations | Connect BuildNinja with tools and workflows that improve the customer experience. |\n| Co-marketing | Create useful demonstrations, guides, or activities around shared customer needs. |\n| Implementation and training | Help teams get started and build confidence in operating their environment. |\n| Technology alliances | Explore complementary products and a clear joint use case. |\n\n### Turn a product conversation into a customer outcome.\n\nA useful partnership can create opportunities to extend your services, support implementation work, and bring a relevant solution to the teams you serve.\n\nWe can discuss product guidance, technical enablement, architecture questions, and joint go-to-market opportunities as part of defining the relationship.\n\n### Start with a focused pilot.\n\n1. **Tell us who you serve.** Share the customer profile and the CI/CD need you see.\n2. **Define the opportunity.** Agree on the use case, responsibilities, and what success would look like.\n3. **Evaluate together.** Start with a practical pilot before planning a broader partnership.\n\n### Tell us where you see a fit.\n\n| Field | Label or helper copy |\n| --- | --- |\n| Partnership type | Technology Partner · Reseller / Channel Partner · System Integrator |\n| Full name | Your full name |\n| Company email | Your business email address |\n| Phone | Country code and phone number |\n| Message | Tell us about your company, the customers you serve, and how you would like to work together. |\n\n**Submit action:** Discuss a partnership  \n**Submitting:** Sending your enquiry…  \n**Validation — type:** Choose a partnership type.  \n**Validation — name:** Enter your name.  \n**Validation — email:** Enter a valid company email address.  \n**Validation — phone:** Enter a valid phone number with country code.  \n**Validation — message:** Tell us about the partnership you have in mind.  \n**Success:** Thanks for sharing your idea. Your enquiry has been received, and we will reply by email.  \n**Error:** Your enquiry could not be sent. Please try again or contact our team.\n\n### A useful partnership starts with a customer need.\n\nLet's understand yours.\n\n**Action:** Discuss a partnership  \n**Alternative:** [Contact the BuildNinja team](https://www.buildninja.io/contact)"
  },
  "release-notes/ai-built-in": {
    "title": "Launch Release Note",
    "seo": "BuildNinja Release Update | AI Built In",
    "description": "BuildNinja now includes AI for log analysis, configuration explanations, and build-risk guidance, with free and prepaid credits.",
    "content": "### BuildNinja now comes with AI.\n\nGet help understanding build information within the product. Explore assistance across logs, configurations, contextual chat, and AI Runner reports.\n\n### What's new.\n\n#### Build-log analysis\n\nAsk AI to interpret the log from a build and suggest areas to investigate.\n\n#### Configuration explanations\n\nGet an explanation of a configuration's steps and settings to help you understand how it works.\n\n#### AI Runner and build analysis reports\n\nAdd an AI Runner execution step to analyze repository code changes. Open Build Results → AI Analysis to explore the risk gauge, severity filters, and file-level findings. Configure the threshold and server-error behavior for the step.\n\n#### Contextual AI chat\n\nContinue the investigation in the AI side panel with the relevant build or configuration context.\n\nAI responses support investigation and can be incomplete or incorrect. Review the underlying information before making changes.\n\n### How AI usage works.\n\nSupported AI features are available in Growth and Shogun. Requests draw from a credit balance.\n\nEligible new accounts can claim a one-time allowance of 500,000 free credits. USD top-ups are available at $10 for 2.5 million, $25 for 7 million, and $50 for 15 million credits, before applicable taxes.\n\nPurchased credits are valid for 12 months. AI requests use a separate credit balance. At zero, new requests pause. An AI Runner step can affect the build result according to its configured failure threshold and server-error policy.\n\n[Read the pricing details](https://www.buildninja.io/pricing#kenzo-ai-credits)\n\n### Quality settings.\n\nChoose Economy, Balanced, or Best for a request, or use your app's default. Credit use varies with the setting, the submitted context, and the response.\n\n### Getting started.\n\n1. Follow the installation or upgrade guidance for this release.\n2. Complete the account configuration and claim or add credits.\n3. Open a supported build or configuration workflow and try the AI action.\n\nAI requests require an internet connection and use an external service to process submitted context.\n\n[Installation and setup](https://www.buildninja.io/install) · [AI terms](https://www.buildninja.io/kenzo-ai-terms) · [AI data policy](https://www.buildninja.io/kenzo-ai-data-policy)\n\n### Try it first.\n\nExplore the sample workflows in Dojo. Its shared AI allowance does not deduct credits from your account.\n\n[Open Dojo](https://www.buildninja.io/dojo) · [Get support](https://www.buildninja.io/support)"
  }
